course: dictionary
lesson: 113
title: Admit: owning up and letting in
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: To admit means to agree, often unwillingly, that something is true or that you did something wrong. «Later he admitted he simply did not like scary things.» He did not want to say it, but the truth came out. To admit something is to say yes to the truth.
explain: Admit can also mean to let someone enter a place. «This ticket admits one child.» The ticket lets one child in, so admit means allow in. You will see this meaning on signs and tickets, like «Children under 5 admitted free».
explain: Context tells you which meaning you need. If the sentence is about a mistake or a truth, it is the first meaning. If it is about a ticket or a door, it is the second. Check by swapping in let in or own up to and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Admit also appears in phrases such as admit defeat, I must admit and admitted to hospital. Admitted to hospital means taken in to stay for treatment, not agreed to. «Laughing at your own mistakes makes them easier to admit» uses admit to mean own up to a mistake.
fact: Admit is a verb: admit, admits, admitted, admitting.
fact: «Admit» can mean to own up: to agree that something is true or that you did wrong.
fact: «Admit» can also mean to let in, as in «this ticket admits one child».
fact: To be admitted to hospital means to be taken in to stay there for treatment.
fact: Admitting a mistake honestly is the first step to putting it right, and it builds trust.
exercise: «Later he admitted he simply did not like scary things.» What does admitted mean here? | Ran away quickly | Let into a room | *Agreed, unwillingly, that something was true | Shouted loudly
exercise: A cinema sign says «Children under 5 admitted free». What does admitted mean? | *Let in | Told off | Sent home
exercise: Which phrase means being taken into hospital to stay for treatment? | Admit defeat | *Admitted to hospital | Admit it | I must admit
test: Which sentence uses admit to mean let in? | «He admitted he had broken the window.» | «Later he admitted he did not like scary things.» | *«This ticket admits one child.» | «Mistakes were made.»
test: Which word could replace admit in «She admitted she was wrong»? | *Confessed | Hid | Shouted | Forgot
exam: Which meaning fits «Laughing at your own mistakes makes them easier to admit»? | *Own up to | Taken to hospital | Shout about | Let in
